// manager_test.go is the ONE test file internal/manager/delivery is allowed to
// have, and that is the whole reason it is the largest file in this repository.
// arch.CheckFileLayout's testFileNameViolations rule (framework-go/arch/
// filelayout.go) flags EVERY *_test.go in a component package whose name is not
// <impl-leaf>_test.go, so the three 13.5k / 7.8k / 11.2k-line test files that came
// with systemdesign, projectdesign and construction had nowhere to go but here.
//
// It is organised exactly like deliverymanager.go: one banner per rail, in the
// same order (systemDesign, projectDesign, construction), bodies moved verbatim.
// Where the three rails carried byte-identical fixture builders, fake
// constructors or assertion helpers, ONE copy survives and is marked in place;
// where a name was shared but the body differed, every rail's copy is prefixed
// (sd/pd/cs for helpers, Test_SD_/Test_PD_/Test_CS_ for test functions) — the
// rename table is in the stage-4a commit message.
//
// Stage 4b deletes the two co-author blocks outright when the three rails become
// one generic DAG walker, and this file shrinks with them. Until then the size is
// a consequence of the layout rule, not of a test-organisation choice.

